.TH "AEGIS" "1" "May 2026" "aegis 0.1.0-demo" "Aegis Manual"

.SH NAME
aegis-snapshot-rescan - Re-query the vulnerability feed for all saved deps and report newly-disclosed advisories


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBaegis snapshot rescan [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
rescan re-queries OSV/GHSA for every dep in aegis.lock regardless of
when it was last enriched. It then diffs against the previously stored
advisories and reports any that are new since the last run.

.PP
Exits 1 when new advisories are found — suitable for a daily cron job
that pages on fresh CVEs affecting already-installed deps.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for rescan

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	emit machine-readable JSON


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB-v\fP, \fB--verbose\fP[=false]
	enable debug-level structured logging to stderr


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBaegis-snapshot(1)\fP
